Every page under `packages/site/src/lib/plans`, `updates` and `stories` opens
with a `---` block that mdsvex reads as YAML. A new `svx-frontmatter` lint
stage now reads that block out of each file and hands it to a YAML parser. A
block that does not parse fails the lint with the file, the line, the column,
the parser's own message, and the offending source line.

## the failure this replaces

mdsvex does not error on a frontmatter block it cannot parse. It emits a module
with no `metadata` export. Nothing notices until the collection loaders run at
prerender: `updates.ts` throws by hand, and `plans.ts` and `stories.ts`
dereference `mod.metadata.id` and hit a TypeError. All three run inside
`nix build .#site`, so the first report was a failed site build in flake-check,
closure-gate and a push shard at once, after the merge.

#4226 did exactly that. One line of an update entry:

```yaml
- label: index#4218 (git-guard: mutating commands in a protected checkout)
```

A plain YAML scalar cannot contain `: `. The parser reads `git-guard:` as the
start of a nested mapping, the block fails, and one prose line takes the whole
site build down. `nix run .#lint` passed on that file before this change.

## a parser, not a pattern

The stage calls a real YAML reader rather than matching a regex. The whole
class here is YAML behaving in a way the person writing prose did not expect,
so a pattern that covers the colon case would still pass the next surprise
while looking like a gate.

What it reports on the #4226 line:

```
packages/site/src/lib/updates/worktree-gate-covers-bash.svx:9:33: frontmatter YAML does not parse: mapping values are not allowed in this context
  - label: index#4218 (git-guard: mutating commands in a protected checkout)
```

The stage runs in 0.5 seconds over all three collections.

## not covered

The stage checks that the block parses and that it parses to a mapping. It does
not check which fields are present or what types they hold; `site-ids` already
covers `id` and `number`, and the loaders check the rest at build time. It also
uses a different YAML implementation from mdsvex's, so a construct the two read
differently would slip through. Every `.svx` in the repo today parses under
both.
